== (i) clustering: the seal reaches every background ==
  20 valid processes (d = 4), seal word '0110', separation n = 32:
  max |p(u gap^n w)/(p(u) p(w)) - 1| over ALL backgrounds
  |u| <= 6: 3.7e-03
  second transfer eigenvalue (rate): median 0.648
  -> clustering holds at the spectral-gap rate: the seal's
     action is nonvanishing on EVERY background of the
     sector - (E-bg) receipted.  The proof needs only
     primitivity of the sector transfer (the DEFINITION of a
     sector, via P16's Frobenius structure) + p(w_seal) > 0
     (P18 R4).

== (ii) the control: wrong-sector backgrounds give zero ==
  reducible ledger (sector 1: only 1s; sector 2: only 0s):
  background u = '00' (sector 2), seal w = '11' (sector 1):
  p(u gap^n w) at n = 1, 4, 16: [0.0, 0.0, 0.0]
  -> ZERO identically: no separation rescues a seal whose
     sector the background excludes.  (E-bg) is a per-sector
     statement - exactly the scope at which the collapse
     lemma operates (sectors are where superselection lives).
